* Generate 32 hexadecimal characters
OpenSSL uses its cryptographic random generator. Each random byte becomes two hex characters.
@code bash
openssl rand -hex 16
@end

* Generate an exact number of hexadecimal characters (Bash)
@code bash
length=27
random_hex=$(openssl rand -hex "$(((length + 1) / 2))")
printf '%s\n' "${random_hex:0:length}"
@end
Choose a positive length. The extra character for an odd length is trimmed; the output includes a trailing newline.
Do not use `$RANDOM` hashed with MD5 for secrets.

Related: {:generate-password:}[generate password]. Reference: {https://docs.openssl.org/3.0/man1/openssl-rand/}[openssl rand].
